ebe8848d (2245 1793567441000 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f16b") (src . "outline: the rows the text is printed from, after the text\n\nA program that wanted the outline had to parse the text a person reads:\none line per block, the id and the label, a conflict mark, an orphan\nword, an orphans section, and the optional keyword and signature\ncolumns, each a printing rule the reader had to know. The answer now\ncarries the rows the text is printed from, so a renderer or an editor\nreads the outline as data and the text stays what it always was. This is\nthe second slice of the --ast design, after read --ast; spans and the\nslugs index follow.\n\noutline answers (ok (text \"...\") (rows <row> ...) ...): the rows are the\nsecond element, present even when there are none, and every clause after\nthem (stale and via with --with-signatures, the receipt, working with\n--working, the dispatcher's incomplete) keeps its old order. A row is\n(row <id> <kind> <mode> <path> <label> <depth> <mark> <orphan> <group>\n(conflicts (<field> ...)) [(keywords \"<s>\")] [(signature \"<s>\")]): kind,\nmode and path are the view's values, #f when absent and a contested\nfield's (conflict ...) datum; label is what the line prints after the\nid; depth the line's level; mark the structural conflict's mark or #f;\norphan #t for an orphan; group tree or orphans, the section the line is\nunder; conflicts the fields whose value is contested, in the view's\norder, the position not repeated. The two optional clauses are there\nexactly when the line prints that column. The human form leaves the rows\nout, as render keeps only incomplete, via and stale after a text clause.\n\nrpc.sc: outline-rows is the one walk, exported: each row reads its\nblock's view once and every element comes from that record; label-of\nreplaces title-of and takes the fetched record, the complete sorted\nstructural rows and the id, so an unnamed code block is numbered among\nall of its siblings whatever depth it is listed at. outline-rows keeps\nthe drawn-once rule for a cyclic row the tree relocated.\nrender-outline-rows, exported, prints the text from the rows alone, byte\nfor byte the old listing: orphans: before the first row of that group,\nno orphan word on that group's roots, the word after the mark on a tree\nrow that is also an orphan. outline-text stays as the wrapper of the\ntwo, and outline-answer puts the text first and the rows second.\nview.sc's header names label-of. The README describes the clause and the\nrow.\n\nTests: test/outline-rows.sc, new, 27 rows over two stores (the main one\nwith a contested title and path, a working writer, a daemon; cli1's\npinned store). OR-1 the text clause is the rows rendered, plain, with\n--depth, --with-keywords, --with-signatures and --working, and the\nin-process rows equal the answer's; OR-2 the view values, the contested\npath as its conflict datum, the labels written out and equal to the text\nline, the orphan and conflict roots on both stores, the conflicts list;\nOR-3 --depth 1 and --depth 0, the keyword and signature clauses exactly\nwhere the text prints the column; OR-4 the pinned bytes of cli1's store\nand of the base tree's CLI, and the human form the text alone; OR-5\nthrough a daemon the text, the rows and exactly the old clauses in their\norder, from the CLI (plain, with signatures) and the MCP shell (plain,\nworking, both), the daemon's rows the in-process ones, a refused working\nview with no rows clause, an incomplete store, and the rows of --working\nthe working view's: a drafted new file's holder at depth 0 and its\npieces under it, none of them in the committed rows; OR-6\nrender-outline-rows on constructed rows; OR-8 a source census of\noutline-rows, view-of once, state-outline once, no state-read and no\ntitle-of, label-of called with the record view-of answered; OR-8b as\nmany rows as live blocks and no id twice. The migrated assertions:\nq8-report's two checks compare the text without the rows and the row ids\nin order, daemon-e1's three string pins and read-receipt's heads gain\nthe clause, supply's clauses-after-text leaves the rows out and its\ncontrol asserts the clause was there. liveness LV-6 reads left-out when\nthe guard's expect file lists describe or outline, one printed line per\nlisted verb; the expect file lists outline, to be emptied by the\nfollow-up commit once this is the base. rows-baseline takes the new\nfixture, the four moved hashes and liveness's line count (46 to 48). Red\nfirst on the base product with these tests: 21 of 27 rows, the six green\nthe three SETUP rows, OR-4's two pins and OR-5's refusal pin. Fifteen\nmutants each red their rows: the walk without its orphans branch, the\nrows clause without the orphan rows, a contested path as #f, a raw title\nfor the label, the orphan word folded into the mark, the group read from\ndepth and orphan, no contested fields, the text clause dropped, the rows\nbefore the text, keywords on rows that print none, the receipt before\nthe rows, a second view read for the label, state-read for keywords,\norphans not filtered by what the tree drew, and the handler answering\n--working from the committed reduction. Reviewed in two rounds: the\nfirst found no fault but a stated limit, that no row showed the working\nrows came from the working view, met by the new-file row and its mutant\non the second freeze; the second no objection from either reviewer.\n\nGate on an isolated copy of the tree (242 fixtures): the known pair red\n(f0-ondemand COST-1 over its budget, startup-ratio C1/C3) and\nclient-start CS-9, whose socket path under this gate's scratch root is\nthree bytes past the sun_path limit (93 plus the 13 a start reserves,\nagainst 104), so socket-path-too-long answers before socket-dir-missing;\nthe row fails on the base too under the same root and passes on both\ntrees under a shorter one, an environment reading recorded for the\nfixture; three python fixtures run; row baseline hashes all the\ndescribed versions, the line counts the ten drift names of the previous\ngate; no process of the run left; source alternation against the base\nmin ratio 0.9974 and alternation of the compiled product median 0.9988\n(p10 ratios 1.0136, 0.9988, 0.9967), both within 1%.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 586))))
