d690db69 (2264 1793576044517 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f413") (src . "test: the socket of a start row under the socket root, with a static row\n\nclient-start's CS-9 order row, a store that is not there given a socket\nin a directory that is not there, built that socket under the fixture's\nscratch root, so its path was as long as the directory the run was\nstarted in. A socket path has to fit sun_path (104 bytes here) and a\nstart reserves 13 more for the daemon's private name; under the gate\nroot of the previous landing the path was three bytes past that, and\nsocket-path-too-long answered before socket-dir-missing, on the base\nas on the tree. The row now builds its socket under sock-here, the\nrunner's socket root, which is short by construction; no-such-dir is\nstill absent, so the row reaches the directory refusal it is about.\n\ntmp-paths.sc gains the section \"the socket root\": scratch-sockets reads\nevery Scheme file as code with Chez's reader, annotations kept, and\ncounts a form (string-append <name> ... \"<s>.sock\" ...) whose first\noperand is one of here, scratch-base, scratch, root, dir or work as a\nviolation, reporting the line the form starts on; a comment is not a\nform and a string holding that text is a string. A line pattern cannot\nsay where a form ends: the one tried read change-stream-guard's two\nforms on one line, a scratch path and then a socket under its socket\nroot, as one. The limits are stated in the header: an unlisted name, a\nhelper, a format string or a variable holding the scratch root's\nsuffix is not seen. TP-S1 asserts more than 100 Scheme files read, more\nthan 20 socket forms seen (a string-append with a \"<s>.sock\" operand,\nwhatever its first operand), no hit and no unreadable file, so an\nempty list cannot be a walk that read nothing; its control plants six\nforms in one text and wants hits at lines 2, 5 and 7 (a nested\noperand, a form across two lines) with five forms seen, the comment\nnot among them and the socket form beside a scratch path seen and not\na hit.\n\nReadings, each predicted before its run: with the new tmp-paths.sc on\nthe base's client-start.sc, TP-S1 alone is red and lists exactly\nclient-start.sc:598; under scratch roots of 91 and 90 bytes the base\nanswers the CS-9 order row socket-path-too-long and the tree is 35 of\n35; four mutants of scratch-sockets (the name test dropped, here left\nout of the names, the line taken from the first operand, the nested\nwalk dropped) each red their row, the third after the two-line form\njoined the control; ascii-only green. rows-baseline moves\nclient-start's hash and tmp-paths' hash and counts, to 49 rows, 124\nlines. Reviewed in one round, no objection from either reviewer.\n\nStage on an isolated copy of the tree, on the pin's igropyr (the one\nin the pin's source tree): 242 fixtures run, not green only the known\npair, f0-ondemand (COST-1, median 835 ms against a budget of 637) and\nstartup-ratio (C1 unreadable, C3 (#f #t)); client-start 35 of 35 and\ntmp-paths 49 rows green; python fixtures 3, none among the not-green.\nRow baseline: every hash as the table describes; line counts differ\nfor the same ten fixtures as the previous landing's gate, liveness\n41/48->41/45 among them. No process carrying the run's token is left.\nSource alternation min ratio 0.9922; no compiled alternation,\ntest-only.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 590))))
